LOCUS       origin_wrap_join         500 bp    DNA     circular SYN 28-APR-2026
DEFINITION  Synthetic plasmid for the BioPython complement(join(1..N,M..L))
            origin-wrap encoding. NOT a real construct.
ACCESSION   origin_wrap_join_synth
VERSION     origin_wrap_join_synth
COMMENT     regression fixture for "complement-strand origin-wrap not
            detected" bug. A plasmid URA3 case surfaced this — BioPython
            (and other tools) sort the parts of `complement(join(...))`
            ascending when the feature wraps the origin. Detection requires
            sequence topology + length, NOT just the location string.

            Three CDSs cover the cases:
              1. ura3_like — origin-wrap encoded as complement(join(1..50,451..500)).
                 The exact shape the parser must detect.
              2. interior_splice — complement(join(100..150,300..400)).
                 Real interior splicing on circular sequence (NOT a wrap).
              3. forward_wrap — single-segment 451..50 form via standard
                 origin-spanning notation. Sanity baseline.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     CDS             complement(join(1..50,451..500))
                     /label="ura3_like"
                     /note="origin-wrapping CDS, complement strand,
                     BioPython-style serialization (parts ascending)"
     CDS             complement(join(100..150,300..400))
                     /label="interior_splice"
                     /note="real interior splicing, NOT a wrap (parts don't
                     touch sequence boundaries)"
     CDS             join(451..500,1..50)
                     /label="forward_wrap"
                     /note="forward-strand origin-wrap, standard physical-order
                     serialization. Existing parser detects this."
